1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
The cheapest insurance for a product launch costs

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
one hour and zero dollars.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:10,500
It's called a premortem, and here's exactly how

4
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:12,000
to run one.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Most launch risk reviews fail for one reason:

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
when you ask a hopeful team 'what could

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,500
go wrong', they protect the plan.

8
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:34,500
Optimism wins, and the real concerns stay in

9
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,000
people's heads.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,473
The premortem flips it.

11
00:00:38,473 --> 00:00:43,418
You don't ask if it could fail —

12
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:46,509
you state that it did.

13
00:00:46,509 --> 00:00:51,455
It's six months from now, the launch was

14
00:00:51,455 --> 00:00:54,545
a flop, that's a fact.

15
00:00:54,545 --> 00:00:59,491
Now ask everyone, individually and silently, to write

16
00:00:59,491 --> 00:01:01,964
down every reason why.

17
00:01:01,964 --> 00:01:06,909
Prospective hindsight gives people permission to name what

18
00:01:06,909 --> 00:01:10,000
they were afraid to say.

19
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,125
Facilitate it cleanly.

20
00:01:12,125 --> 00:01:17,792
Two minutes silent and solo first — that

21
00:01:17,792 --> 00:01:23,458
protects the junior and the quiet voices from

22
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:27,708
the loudest person in the room.

23
00:01:27,708 --> 00:01:33,375
Then round-robin, one reason each, no debate, until

24
00:01:33,375 --> 00:01:36,208
the list is empty.

25
00:01:36,208 --> 00:01:41,875
Cluster, and pick the two or three you

26
00:01:41,875 --> 00:01:44,000
can de-risk now.

27
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,923
Done right, a premortem doesn't make your team

28
00:01:48,923 --> 00:01:49,538
negative.

29
00:01:49,538 --> 00:01:52,000
It makes them honest.

30
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,923
You catch the dependency nobody owned and the

31
00:01:56,923 --> 00:02:01,846
assumption everyone agreed with too fast — for

32
00:02:01,846 --> 00:02:06,769
the price of one meeting instead of one

33
00:02:06,769 --> 00:02:08,000
failed launch.

34
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,538
Here's your move: before your next launch, block

35
00:02:13,538 --> 00:02:17,000
sixty minutes and run this.

36
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,538
Comment the launch you're about to ship and

37
00:02:22,538 --> 00:02:26,000
I'll send the premortem checklist.
